{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/722812-ex3-supernal-ability-list-of-favorite-charms-to-get-your-solar-on","id":722812,"title":"[Ex3] Supernal Ability, list of favorite charms to get your Solar on","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-24T06:59:39-07:00","id":722812,"title":"[Ex3] Supernal Ability, list of favorite charms to get your Solar on","content":"Lore: God's Shrike is frankly one of my favorite high levels charm. You essentially get to declare what is going to happen. Why fight when you can have behemoth walking the earth? Potentially even more ridiculous with excellency used.<br /> <br /> Athletics: Nine Aeons Thew, essentially no matter how heavy something is, you will succeed in lifting it. You want to make hercules, Kratos? that's your charm.<br /> <br /> Awareness: Eye of the Unconquered Sun, it comes with so many goodies, it is almost a discount compared to all the other charms you would need to dematerialize spirits etc... all that within a ridiculous range of you.<br /> <br /> Brawl: Ascendant Battle Visage: this is super saiyan and I'm not even kidding.<br /> <br /> Resistance: Aegis of Invincible Might, literally what it says on the can, making you a soak monster.<br /> <br /> So what are your favorites or think that are worth the investment in a supernal ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T07:09:58-07:00","id":722869,"title":"","content":"Lore also lets you get wyld shaping technique early, which is tempting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T08:33:19-07:00","id":723135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/722812-ex3-supernal-ability-list-of-favorite-charms-to-get-your-solar-on#post722812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Athletics: Nine Aeons Thew, essentially no matter how heavy something is, you will succeed in lifting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it just lets you <i>attempt </i>it, but if you want to do something bad enough that's not a problem. A quick calculation reveals that using its prerequisites you can rack up a truly preposterous number of successes.<br /> <br /> An Essence 5, Athletics 5 character with an applicable speciality and Mighty Thew, using Increasing Strength Exercise, Thunder's Might, Aegis of Unstoppable Force and Nine Aeons Thew rolls 34 dice, rerolling all non-successes, doubling 7s and reducing difficulty by 2. I make that an average success rate of 43, allowing the Solar to succeed at tasks of <i>difficulty 45 on average</i>.<br /> <br /> For reference, at dificulty 20 a character can smash through ten feet of rock or tear open a crevasse in the earth with his hands. I invite you to imagine what would be possible at difficulty 45.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://bbsimg.ngfiles.com/1/23876000/ngbbs4f7e05dfc7b71.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Lore is my favourite because there is just so much it opens up. Extra evocations, Essence-transferring group support, prophetic destruction of major cities...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 10-24-2015, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T17:11:57-07:00","id":724530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/722812-ex3-supernal-ability-list-of-favorite-charms-to-get-your-solar-on?p=723135#post723135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"http://bbsimg.ngfiles.com/1/23876000/ngbbs4f7e05dfc7b71.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>^_^<br /> <br /> I think Unbowed Willow Meditation is the first Charm that made me say &quot;oh shit&quot; aloud, but at that time the Supernal Ability mechanic hadn't been written yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T17:21:28-07:00","id":724558,"title":"","content":"Nine Aeons Thew. Ascendant Battle Visage. Deadly Predator Method (which feels like a scenelong rather than Indefinite, but whatever).<br /> <br /> I was honestly a little angry that these Charms didn't exist back when I played my Dawn. Instead of forgetting my awesome fire hyena, she could've turned into a defining element of my combat style!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T20:00:25-07:00","id":724870,"title":"","content":"Athletics makes me super happy since i tend to make pint size bruisers. The image of a little girl throwing a mountain amuses me. <br /> <br /> Master Plan Meditation - I KNEW THAT WOULD HAPPEN so i compensated... love that charm in larceny.<br /> <br /> False image feint....<br /> <br /> Ninja Log <br /> <br /> nuff said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T20:02:25-07:00","id":724874,"title":"","content":"Survival for those sweet, sweet Familiar Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}